course: dictionary
lesson: 2080
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word construction can mean the work of building, a thing that has been built, the way words are put together in grammar, or an exact drawing in maths. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context.
explain: «You never go inside the fence of a construction site, because machines, holes and falling things are dangerous.» Here a construction site is a place where things are being built. The clues are the fence, the machines and the holes, so you know it is a place to stay out of.
explain: «Artists lightly sketch big simple shapes first; light guide lines drawn first and rubbed out later are called construction lines.» In this sentence construction lines are not buildings at all. They are faint pencil lines used to guide a drawing, which is why they are rubbed out later.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Construction means the work of building things such as houses, roads and bridges.
fact: A construction can also be something that has been built, or a structure made of parts.
fact: In grammar, a construction is the way words are put together in a sentence.
fact: In maths, a construction is a drawing made exactly with a ruler and compass.
fact: «Under construction» means being built right now, and a «construction site» is where building work happens.
fact: Never go inside a construction site: it is dangerous because of machines, holes and falling things.
exercise: «You never go inside the fence of a construction site, because machines, holes and falling things are dangerous.» What is a construction site? | A shop that sells fences | A park with swings and a slide | A school playground at break time | *A place where things are being built
exercise: In maths, what is a construction? | *A drawing made exactly with a ruler and compass | A type of cloud | A bridge made of paper | A sentence with a missing word
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Artists lightly sketch big simple shapes first» that means to draw roughly and quickly. | shapes | *sketch | simple | artists
test: A sign says «Road under construction». What does it mean? | The road is a short cut to the park | *The road is being built or repaired right now | The road has been painted a bright colour | The road is finished and open to cars
test: In grammar, what does construction mean? | A drawing made with a ruler | *The way words are put together in a sentence | A machine used on a building site | A type of paper for craft
exam: Why must you keep out of a construction site? | Because it is quiet and dark | Because it is a good place to play | Because the fence is painted red | *Because machines, holes and falling things are dangerous
